@@ -28,6 +28,39 @@ Tasks shows background work across your conversations. A browser window can clos
 
 The passwordless profile chooser is for this local synthetic workspace. The app binds to loopback. Each profile has its own bots, chats, saved entries, and task activity. A bot's memory is scoped to that bot.
 
+## What to expect
+
+**Setup.** Once a token is saved in Setup, or a valid `PROVIDER_TOKEN` is set, the app is set up for every person. If `PROVIDER_TOKEN` is set but the provider refuses it, Setup says so without showing it, and you can save a token there instead.
+
+**Bots and conversations.**
+- A new bot starts with one empty conversation, listed as **Untitled conversation**. After the first message, a conversation is named after that message, with line breaks and runs of spaces made single spaces, cut to 56 characters. The newest conversation is listed first.
+- When two conversations of a bot would have the same name, the later one gets a number, for example **How many orders can you see? (2)**. Pointing at a conversation shows your latest message in it.
+- Your unsent text and reading position are kept for each conversation while the browser tab stays open, including across a reload. A new tab starts with an empty message box.
+- Dark mode is remembered by the browser, so it applies to every person who uses that browser.
+
+**Limits.** Bot names and saved-entry names take up to 80 characters, and saved-entry text and memory text up to 12,000; those boxes stop accepting text at the limit. A message longer than 12,000 characters is not sent: an alert says so and your text stays in the box. Spaces at the start and end of names and text are removed when saved. An action request over 64 KB is refused with "That request is too large."
+
+**Saved instructions and tasks.**
+- They belong to you and are shared by all your bots; other people do not see them.
+- **Use** copies the instruction's current text onto the open bot. Editing or deleting the saved entry later does not change a bot that already uses it until you use it again. **Clear instructions**, under the active instructions, returns the open bot to having none and keeps its conversations.
+- Saving under a name that is already saved, without choosing **Edit** first, is refused, and the saved entry stays as it was.
+
+**Memory.** Asking the bot to remember a fact it already has (capitals aside) adds no second copy. Asking it to forget removes a fact only when you give the whole fact (capitals aside). The reply says it has forgotten either way, so check Memory.
+
+**Records and changes.**
+- Questions and changes use the record's own field names, such as `status`. A field written in other capitals is not matched: **What is the STATUS of ORD-1001** gets "ORD-1001 has no STATUS.", and **set the STATUS of ORD-1001 to closed** proposes nothing. Its Change result names the right field.
+- After **Update ORD-1001**, give the field and the value in one answer, such as **the status to closed**. Any other answer, such as just **status**, is echoed back and the question is not asked again; send **Update ORD-1001** again. Other phrasings, such as "Could you close order ORD-1001 for me?", are echoed too; say **set the status of ORD-1001 to closed**.
+- In Proposed changes, a value that contains `·`, `→` or quotation marks, or that could be read as a number or as empty (`∅`), is shown in quotation marks.
+- A number larger than 9007199254740991 cannot be stored exactly, so no change is proposed for it. The id, type and readers of a record cannot be changed through the chat.
+- **Confirm changes** applies nothing if a field no longer has the value the proposal started from, or if a new order's number has been taken; the Change result asks for a fresh proposal.
+
+**Background tasks.**
+- Several long tasks can run in one conversation. **Add step** adds its step to the end of the most recently started task that is still running in that conversation.
+- **Since you were away** compares with the last time this browser showed your workspace. It lists tasks that finished or were cancelled after that, and every task that is running, failed or interrupted.
+- While the page waits for the server to answer an action (normally a few milliseconds), it ignores other clicks. A **Cancel task** pressed at that moment does nothing; the task still shows Running with its Cancel task button, so press it again.
+- If the page cannot reach the server, an alert says that what you see is the last known state, until the server answers again.
+- If the data folder cannot be written, actions are refused with an alert, and a reply or task that could not save its progress stops and shows as failed. Once the folder can be written again, use **Retry** or **Retry task**.
+
